# Doom (W11-S05) started from the Go kernel's console with the Freedoom WAD
# on the FAT disk at /mnt. Doom draws only on screen, so steps after its
# start wait for pixels (waitpixel) or for time: the title, then Enter four
# times (menu, New Game, the episode, the skill) into E1M1, a walk forward,
# and Quit Game from the menu (Escape, up wraps to the last item, Enter, y).
# A fixed sleep before the E1M1 dump caught Doom's screen melt half done
# when the level's first frames were slow. The melt drops columns at random
# speeds, so each dump waits for the pixels nearest the bottom.
wait burrow> 
type run /bin/doom -iwad /mnt/freedoom1.wad
key ret
wait Auto-scaling
waitpixel 250 560 #ff801c
waitpixel 831 583 #440101
screendump build/screen-doom-title.ppm
key ret
sleep 1
key ret
sleep 1
key ret
sleep 1
key ret
waitpixel 240 575 #8b8b8b
waitpixel 780 535 #9f9f9f
screendump build/screen-doom-e1m1.ppm
key up
key up
key up
sleep 1
key esc
sleep 1
key up
sleep 1
key ret
sleep 1
type y
wait burrow> 
type poweroff
key ret
